                        "entry_id": "49521c05-1eeb-3212-addb-2cb766926435",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dans l’ancienne université de Paris, docteur en théologie qui n’était attaché à aucune maison."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2794921b-241b-3006-a978-f2d1190b50fe",
                        "entry_id": "49521c05-1eeb-3212-addb-2cb766926435",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Personne à qui tous les lieux sont indifférents et qui se trouve partout à son aise."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9708993c-4687-3394-8649-72f2225eb352",
                        "entry_id": "49521c05-1eeb-3212-addb-2cb766926435",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Espèce dont l’aire de répartition est très étendue, voire mondiale."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dfee4cdb-6488-4403-9b29-60d2e78e9eb5",
                                "sense_id": "9708993c-4687-3394-8649-72f2225eb352",
                                "text": "[…]; par sédimentation mixte, la consolidation se poursuit et la bande littorale se trouve occupée successivement par certaines ubiquistes des associations d’Hélophytes que pénètrent plus tard les premiers noyaux arbustifs de Salix et à Alnus glutinosa."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "14b9352b-dc1d-4292-b19d-0cf7fbce0b11",
                        "source_entry_id": "49521c05-1eeb-3212-addb-2cb766926435",
                        "target_lang_word": "allgegenwärtig",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "allgegenwärtig",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "351cb625-4aa4-3e79-8fc7-396ba48964aa",
                                        "entry_id": "f1ac17b6-ee09-3056-bb03-b51dde53bee8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "überall und jederzeit vorhanden"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ffdf3401-531a-48f2-9bce-80841c559de3",
                                                "sense_id": "351cb625-4aa4-3e79-8fc7-396ba48964aa",
                                                "text": "„Aus der Besprechung ging klar hervor, dass dem guten Kritiker nicht im Geringsten aufgefallen war, dass das Verschwinden, auf das der Buchtitel hinweist, in Wirklichkeit nicht auf die Menschen anspielt, die im Roman verschwinden, sondern darauf, dass in ihm der sonst allgegenwärtige Buchstabe E nicht vorkommt.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f5763531-7763-45e3-b0b3-d5f8c1359d26",
                                                "sense_id": "351cb625-4aa4-3e79-8fc7-396ba48964aa",
                                                "text": "„Den allgegenwärtigen Terror bekommen auch die Soldaten der UN-Mission Minusma zu spüren, die in Gao und anderen Städten den Friedensprozess überwachen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c203f6a-6acb-4dc2-8df3-41bbf07c9a0e",
                                                "sense_id": "351cb625-4aa4-3e79-8fc7-396ba48964aa",
                                                "text": "„Der Herztod ist in Deutschland allgegenwärtig. Bei mindestens 60.000 Menschen im Jahr hört das Herz plötzlich auf zu pumpen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "99a98d19-2d97-4d60-aaca-1f5415ef6f39",
                        "source_entry_id": "49521c05-1eeb-3212-addb-2cb766926435",
                        "target_lang_word": "ubiquitous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ubiquitous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e964613-b452-3006-b03e-85b348af8da5",
                                        "entry_id": "0b5237f7-dbd9-3199-8759-344579f92bec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Being everywhere at once: omnipresent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31a7d3da-edd7-4dc0-ab7c-110bfafa8060",
                                                "sense_id": "0e964613-b452-3006-b03e-85b348af8da5",
                                                "text": "In Christianity, Hinduism, and Judaism, God is ubiquitous."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "308be6e5-7be5-38eb-8f32-790a92312c03",
                                        "entry_id": "0b5237f7-dbd9-3199-8759-344579f92bec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Appearing to be everywhere at once; being or seeming to be in more than one location at the same time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "508734df-94dc-4189-a1f2-7337a00648e5",
                                                "sense_id": "308be6e5-7be5-38eb-8f32-790a92312c03",
                                                "text": "One of the wild suggestions referred to, as at last coming to be linked with the White Whale in the minds of the superstitiously inclined, was the unearthly conceit that Moby Dick was ubiquitous; that he had actually been encountered in opposite latitudes at one and the same instant of time."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89d428c4-d987-44a4-aea3-33d4848613b4",
                                                "sense_id": "308be6e5-7be5-38eb-8f32-790a92312c03",
                                                "text": "There is much sad evidence, too, of the spoliation and dereliction of vanished industry: tips, slag-heaps and derelict colliery-screens among which the ubiquitous, nomad mountain sheep graze unconcernedly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "332d3f22-d45b-43cb-9648-0cc9eca5c792",
                                                "sense_id": "308be6e5-7be5-38eb-8f32-790a92312c03",
                                                "text": "This deed accomplished, life no longer suffers hopelessly under the terrible mutilations of ubiquitous disaster, battered by time, hideous throughout space; but with its horror visible still, its cries of anguish still tumultuous, it becomes penetrated by an all-suffusing, all-sustaining love, and a knowledge of its own unconquered power."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc2de8a9-ecd6-3d22-8c72-8c73a338bcfe",
                                        "entry_id": "0b5237f7-dbd9-3199-8759-344579f92bec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Widespread; very prevalent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
